From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cofre <cofre@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:56:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [COFRE] Run Metallum on iOS for Minecraft 26.2

Reason: The 26.2 Metallum (a12ffb3) installs its CAMetalLayer on the GLFW Cocoa NSView, waits for frames with Objective-C completion blocks (FFM upcall stubs, which SIGBUS on iOS), calls the macOS-only displaySyncEnabled and targets the macOS MSL platform. On iOS (Air) it must use the launcher's published CAMetalLayer, poll command-buffer status, drain a per-frame autorelease pool, target iOS MSL and use the launcher's signed SPIRV-Cross. It also releases render pipeline states immediately on close and can rebuild a closed pipeline from its released descriptor (resource reload use-after-free), and compiles shader functions without the lock 26.3 added (5bee03e).
Drop when: Cofre stops shipping Metal for Minecraft 26.2, or Metallum ships these fixes on a 26.2 branch.
---
 build.gradle                                  |  4 ++
 .../com/metallum/render/MetalBackend.java     | 56 ++++++++++++-------
 .../metallum/render/MetalCommandEncoder.java  | 50 ++++++++++-------
 .../render/MetalCompiledRenderPipeline.java   | 19 ++++++-
 .../render/MetalCrossShaderCompiler.java      |  9 ++-
 .../java/com/metallum/render/MetalDevice.java |  2 +-
